message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "polymarket-coherence: price coherence in mutually-exclusive prediction markets"
abstract: >-
  A small, reproducible study of price coherence in Polymarket's mutually-exclusive
  (negRisk) events, extended to a cross-market test against Kalshi. It shows that the
  large multi-outcome coherence "violations" a naive observer sees are governed by
  liquidity structure and market microstructure, not exploitable mispricing, and that
  the only genuine sub-$1 lock windows are rare, marginal (<=2.7% gross), and confined
  to the smallest dense fields. All numbers are reproducible from committed public data
  with no keys or wallet.
